---
title: Sweet and Sour Chicken
servings: 4
course: Main
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
prep time: 20m
cook time: 15m
cuisine: Chinese
tags:
- poultry
- main-course
- savoury
- chinese
---

Drain the @pineapple chunks in juice{1%tin × 425 g}, keeping all the juice. Put the @cornflour{2%tbsp} in a large bowl and stir in 3 tbsp of the pineapple juice to make a smooth paste. Add the remaining juice and @water{150%ml}, then stir in the @dark soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @white wine vinegar{2%tbsp}, @soft light brown sugar{2%tbsp}, @tomato ketchup{2%tbsp}, and @dried chilli flakes{0.5%tsp}, until thoroughly combined. Set aside.

Cut each @chicken breasts{2}(boneless and skinless) into eight or nine even pieces. Heat 1 tbsp of the @sunflower oil{2%tbsp} in a #large non-stick frying pan or wok{} and stir-fry the @onion{1%medium}(cut into 12 wedges) and @peppers{2}(deseeded and cut into 3 cm chunks) for ~{2%minutes} over a high heat.

Add the remaining oil and the chicken to the pan. Stir-fry for ~{2%minutes} until coloured on all sides. Add the @garlic{2%cloves}(crushed), @ginger{25%g}(finely grated), pineapple chunks, and @water chestnuts{1%tin × 225 g}(sliced and drained). Stir-fry for 30 to ~{60%seconds}.

Give the cornflour and pineapple mixture a good stir and add it to the pan with the chicken and vegetables. Stir well, season with some @black pepper{}(freshly ground) and bring to a simmer. Cook for 4 to ~{6%minutes} until the sauce is thickened and glossy and the chicken is tender and cooked throughout, turning the chicken and vegetables a few times. Serve with a small portion of rice.